 surge capacity","18":"Here are some products worth comparing.","15":" Better suited for refrigerator compressors","16":"UPS/EPS functionality:","17":" Useful if you want automatic switchover when utility power fails"}},{"p":"/message/metadata/model_dil_v2/fallbackMarkdown","o":"replace","v":"## Refrigerator backup power supplies\n\nFor keeping a refrigerator running during a power outage, the most practical options are **portable battery power stations**, **battery backup systems with UPS functionality**, and **inverter generators**\\.\n\nA typical household refrigerator may use 100\u2013250 watts while running, but its compressor can briefly require much more power when starting.\n\nFor a battery backup, I recommend looking for\\:\n\n- **Capacity\\:** 1,000\u20132,000 Wh or more\n- **AC output\\:** At least 1,000 W continuous, with adequate compressor startup surge capacity\n- **Pure sine wave inverter\\:** Better suited for refrigerator compressors\n- **UPS/EPS functionality\\:** Useful if you want automatic switchover when utility power fails\n\nHere are some products worth comparing."}],"c":11}  

